--
--   Description
----------------
--   To verify that invalid codes, received while xmit=CONFIGURATION,cause auto-negotiation to restart, and that only Ordered Sets that are four bytes in length,
--   that begin with /K28.5/D21.5 or /K28.5/D2.2/ are treated as valid configuration ordered sets.
-- 
-- Detailed Test Description
----------------------------
-- 1. Initialise the GEM for Gigabit Operation with PCS enabled. Furthermore, Auto-Negotiation is 
--    enabled. 
-- 2. Restart auto-negotiation by resetting bit 9 in the pcs control register
-- 3. Continuously provide one of the stream of /C/ codes noted below.
-- 4. Observe the Config_Reg transmitted by the GEM, monitoring bit 14 (ACK). 
-- 5. Repeat steps (2) through (4) until all patterns noted below have been tested.
--  
-- Test patterns 
-- Part A:
--
--     1./K28.5/D21.5/D0.3/D0.0 ?
--     2./K28.5/D2.2/D0.3/D0.0/K28.5/D2.2/D0.3/D0.0 ?
--
--    Test patterns in part A should result in the device setting bit 14 (ACK) to one after several
--    repetitions of the pattern.
--
-- Part B:
--
--     1./K28.5/D21.5/K28.5/D21.5 ?
--     2./K28.5/D2.2/K28.5/D2.2 ?
--     3./K28.5/D21.5/D0.3 /K28.5/D2.2/D0.3 /K28.5/D21.5/D0.3 /K28.5/D2.2/D0.3 ?
--     4./K28.5/D21.5/D0.3/D0.0/D0.3 /K28.5/D2.2/D0.3/D0.0/D0.3 /K28.5/D21.5/D0.3/D0.0/D0.3 /K28.5/D2.2/D0.3/D0.0/D0.3 ?
--     5./K28.5/D0.3/D0.0 ?
--     6./K28.5/D16.2/K27.7/D16.2 /K28.5/D16.2/K27.7/D16.2 ?
--     7./K27.7/D16.2/K27.7/D16.2 ?
--     8./K27.7/D21.5/D0.3/D0.0 /K27.7/D2.2/D0.3/D0.0 /K27.7/D21.5/D0.3/D0.0 /K27.7/D2.2/D0.3/D0.0 ?
--     9.(Ending RD+) /+K28.5/+D2.2/-D0.3/+D0.0 /+K28.5/-D21.5/-D0.3/+D0.0 ? {D2.2 RD is flipped}
--   10.(Ending RD+) /+K28.5/-D21.5/+D0.3/-D0.0 /-K28.5/+D2.2/-D0.3/+D0.0 ? {1st D0.3 RD is flipped}
--   11.(Ending RD+) /+K28.5/-D21.5/-D0.3/-D0.0 /-K28.5/+D2.2/-D0.3/+D0.0 ? {1st D0.0 RD is flipped}
--   12.(Ending RD+) /+K28.5/-D21.5/-D0.3/+D0.0 /-K28.5/+D2.2/-D0.3/+D0.0 /+K28.5/-D21.5/-D0.3/+D0.0 /+K28.5/-D2.2/+D0.3/-D0.0 /-K28.5/+D21.5/+D0.3/-D0.0
--       /-K28.5/+D2.2/-D0.3/+D0.0 ? {1st -K28.5 is invalid, should be +K28.5}
--   13.(Ending RD+) /+K28.5/-D21.5/-D0.3/+D0.0 /+K28.5/-D2.2/+D0.3/-D0.0 /+K28.5/-D21.5/-D0.3/+D0.0 /+K28.5/-D2.2/+D0.3/-D0.0 /-K28.5/+D21.5/+D0.3/-D0.0
--       /-K28.5/+D2.2/-D0.3/+D0.0 ? {3rd +K28.5 is invalid, should be -K28.5}
--   14.(Ending RD-) /K28.5/D21.5/D0.3 /K28.5/D2.2/D0.3 ? {sequence begins with RD- but ends with RD+}
--
--    Test patterns in part B should result in the device restarting auto-negotiation, resulting in the transmission of a Config_Reg of all zero. Continuous reception of these
--    patterns should prevent the DUT from ever transmitting a non-zero Config_Reg
--
--   Note 1: Ending RD+/- indicates that the current running disparity is either + or - when the pattern is constructed. /+K28.5/ refers to the 10-bit code group for K28.5 from the
--   Current RD+ column of Table 36-2 in the IEEE 802.3 Spec.
--
--   Note 2: To cause the tb_pcs_rx test-bench to be triggered from tb_pcs_tx test-bench
--   the following commands should be used.
--
--  i.e.
--  pcs_an_tx(trx)        0000
--  pcs_an_rx(trx)        c16000c26000c16000c26000
--
--    The trigger field in the pcs_an_tx command should have trx in it.
--    This will cause the tb_pcs_tx test-bench to generate a pulse to trigger the
--    start of the pcs_an_rx command. Then, the trigger field in the pcs_an_rx
--    command should have trx in it.  This will cause the tb_pcs_rx test-bench
--    to trigger off the pulse generated in tb_pcs_tx test-bench.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

